## Remaining uncertainty and review conclusion

The proposal cannot yet certify the 3 GB / 16 GB target, tile decode bounds, end-to-end cancellation latency, atomic saves on shared storage, cross-machine path relocation, or exact interoperability of exported annotations. The chosen architecture remains conditional on a compatibility and fixture spike. This affects whether the proposed readers can ship in v1 and whether external references are adequate for a given project; it does not justify silently accepting ambiguous inputs. The final therefore includes measurable proposed validation criteria and a metadata-only failure route, and labels all such tests UNEXECUTED. No source chain was inferred from a title or PR link alone.